{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:PredictedSpectra.CategoricalProtonUnique","@type":"LeanModule","name":"PredictedSpectra.CategoricalProtonUnique","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalProton.unique_up_to_isotopy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalProton.unique_up_to_isotopy","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/categorical-proton-unique.lean#L54-L71","doc":"**Uniqueness of the categorical proton up to braid isotopy**\n(conditional on the Hecke-normal-form coincidence of\n[`def:categorical-proton`]).\n\nTwo categorical protons with the same Hecke normal form in `H₃(q)` and the\nsame `S₃` colour assignment are equal.  This replaces the earlier\n`Subsingleton CategoricalProton` axiom, which was *false* for the free real\nfields `skein_uu, skein_ud`: distinct Skein data give genuinely distinct\nprotons, so uniqueness holds only conditionally on a shared Hecke normal\nform — exactly the content of the narrative statement. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:categorical-proton-unique","label":"prop:categorical-proton-unique","md":"quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/categorical-proton-unique.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ProtonSameHeckeNF.chirality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ProtonSameHeckeNF.chirality","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/categorical-proton-unique.lean#L52-L52","doc":"Same chirality. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ProtonSameHeckeNF.mass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ProtonSameHeckeNF.mass","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/categorical-proton-unique.lean#L50-L50","doc":"Same derived mass. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ProtonSameHeckeNF.skein_ud","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ProtonSameHeckeNF.skein_ud","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/categorical-proton-unique.lean#L48-L48","doc":"Same pair-Skein mass `S_ud`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ProtonSameHeckeNF.skein_uu","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ProtonSameHeckeNF.skein_uu","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/categorical-proton-unique.lean#L46-L46","doc":"Same pair-Skein mass `S_uu`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ProtonSameHeckeNF.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ProtonSameHeckeNF.mk","kind":"ctor","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/categorical-proton-unique.lean#L44-L44","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ProtonSameHeckeNF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ProtonSameHeckeNF","kind":"class","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/categorical-proton-unique.lean#L35-L52","doc":"**Hecke-normal-form coincidence context.**\n\nTwo categorical protons share the same Hecke normal form in `H₃(q)` and the\nsame `S₃` colour assignment.  By [`def:categorical-proton`] the Hecke normal\nform determines the pair-Skein masses, the derived mass, and the chirality;\nthe `S₃` permutation symmetry on the colour tubes makes the assignment of\n`(u, u, d)` to tube positions irrelevant.  This class records that\ncoincidence as explicit hypotheses, so the uniqueness theorem below is a\nrigorous *conditional* result. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalProton.chirality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalProton.chirality","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/categorical-proton-unique.lean#L33-L33","doc":"Positive crossing chirality (electric charge `+1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalProton.mass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalProton.mass","kind":"def","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/categorical-proton-unique.lean#L31-L31","doc":"Mass `= S_uu + 2·S_ud`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalProton.skein_ud","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalProton.skein_ud","kind":"def","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/categorical-proton-unique.lean#L29-L29","doc":"Pair Skein mass `S_ud`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalProton.skein_uu","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalProton.skein_uu","kind":"def","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/categorical-proton-unique.lean#L27-L27","doc":"Pair Skein mass `S_uu`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalProton.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalProton.mk","kind":"ctor","line":25,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/categorical-proton-unique.lean#L25-L25","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalProton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalProton","kind":"structure","line":20,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/categorical-proton-unique.lean#L20-L33","doc":"Defining data of the categorical proton (mirror of\n[`def:categorical-proton`], `QOU.Torsion.CategoricalProton`): the\ncolour-linked triple `[u, u, d]_c ⋈ L_H` is determined by its pair-Skein\nmasses `(S_uu, S_ud)`, with derived mass `S_uu + 2·S_ud` and positive\ncrossing chirality `+1`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}